    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0151" n="19" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg19"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    Leahy Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 17 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Truman to Prime Minister Churchill
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d17-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d17-f2"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-05-21">21 May 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. Your number 53. …<anchor n="3" xml:id="d17-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>I may, within the next two weeks, have more information bearing on a date and
                    location for the proposed tripartite meeting if Stalin agrees to participate.</p>
                <p>I hope he will agree to come west into Germany or further west, but I am advised
                    that he is not likely to go beyond Soviet controlled, territory.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d17-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d17-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably sent to the United States Naval Attaché, London, via Navy
                    channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f2" n="2" xml:id="d17-f2-content">
                <p>The portion of this message not printed here related to Venezia Giulia. See
                        Truman, <hi rendition="#italic">Year
                        of Decisions</hi>, pp. 250–251.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f3" n="3" xml:id="d17-f3-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="#d16">document No. 16</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
